  "visible_text": "(27 \\cdot 9^{n+1})^3 =\nA. 3^{6n+12}\nB. 3^{6n+15}\nC. 3^{9n+12}\nD. 3^{9n+18}",
  "answer": "B",
  "reasoning": "27 = 3^3 and 9 = 3^2, so 9^{n+1} = (3^2)^{n+1} = 3^{2n+2}. Then 27·9^{n+1} = 3^3·3^{2n+2} = 3^{2n+5}. Raising to the third power gives (3^{2n+5})^3 = 3^{3(2n+5)} = 3^{6n+15}, which corresponds to option B.",
  "raw": "{\"visible_text\": \"(27 \\\\cdot 9^{n+1})^3 =\\nA. 3^{6n+12}\\nB. 3^{6n+15}\\nC. 3^{9n+12}\\nD. 3^{9n+18}\", \"answer\": \"B\", \"reasoning\": \"27 = 3^3 and 9 = 3^2, so 9^{n+1} = (3^2)^{n+1} = 3^{2n+2}. Then 27·9^{n+1} = 3^3·3^{2n+2} = 3^{2n+5}. Raising to the third power gives (3^{2n+5})^3 = 3^{3(2n+5)} = 3^{6n+15}, which corresponds to option B.\"}"
